## Verdict

Before fixes: ready.

Every POUR criterion passes in the live story (keyboard, focus return, inert page, AX tree name, description and heading level, forced colors, 320px reflow, contrast and focus ring in both modes), axe is clean on all stories, check passes, and the behavior spec passes (one load flake that passes alone). The three Low items are a test hardening, a missing IME test, and an owner-accepted native Tab behavior; none blocks stable.

## Status (2026-11-16, after fixes)

- Low 2 (form test flake) closed: the test now waits for the invalid field to take focus after the blocked submit (spec line 617). The dialog spec passed 59 of 59 on two consecutive runs at `--workers=2`.
- Low 3 (no IME test) closed: new test "Escape while an input method is composing neither fires sb-cancel nor closes"; the coordinator confirmed it fails without the `isComposing` guard.
- Low 1 (Tab leaves into browser chrome) stays as owner-accepted Q4.
- The SB-0102 manual-pass wording stays in an accepted decision; SB-0113 already supersedes manual screen-reader passes.

## Status (2026-11-16, after the second round)

Live pass in the real stories with real key presses (Chromium, Storybook on 6117), probes deleted afterwards.

- Tab wraps inside the page: closed. Default (Name, Username, Cancel, Save changes, Close, then Name again), Form, Long content, RTL and No close button (Tab and Shift+Tab alternate between the footer Close and the first control) all wrap in both directions with no focus in browser chrome; Escape still returns focus to the trigger. Nested: the inner dialog cycles Cancel, Done, Close and back, the outer cycles Cancel, Done, Close, Advanced and back, Escape closes the inner first and focus returns to "Advanced...", after which the outer still wraps. Search palette (no close button, one tab stop): Tab and Shift+Tab stay on the input, ArrowDown moves the Command selection, Escape closes and focus returns to the trigger. This replaces Low 1 (Q4, native Tab leaving the page); the APG wrap now holds.
- Title name follows text changes without element references: closed. With `ariaLabelledByElements` removed in the page, the AX tree dialog name went "Edit profile" > "Renamed once" (textContent) > "Renamed once and more" (append) > "Replaced element" (title element replaced), and is empty after the title is removed (a name is then required from aria-label, with the dev warning). The description has no fallback there, as documented. This closes the D2 residual.
- Behavior spec: 62 of 62 passed at `--workers=2`.
- `sketchbook check` is not clean. Open: X1 fails on `spec/decisions/DECISIONS.md` SB-0118: "supersedes unknown SB-0102", because the `Supersedes:` line has a parenthetical after the id (`SB-0102 (only its Watch out ...)`); put only `SB-0102` there and move the scope note to Context or Watch out. D1 and D4 fail for Dialog (and Sidebar) because the contract changed after the last Figma sync and read-back: expected, they need the Figma round. T5 and A1 warnings are unrelated.

Verdict: ready
